**Layer 2: Transcriptomic --- Bulk Expression, Single-Cell, RNA
Velocity**

**What it captures:** Gene expression at bulk and single-cell
resolution. Cell type identification. Transcriptional trajectories
showing cells transitioning toward resistance (RNA velocity). KAALCURA
biological axes per cell population.

**Critical distinction:** Bulk RNA-seq (GDSC, SU2C) gives average
expression across all cells. Single-cell RNA-seq resolves individual
cell states --- essential for identifying pre-resistant populations. RNA
velocity (unspliced/spliced mRNA ratio) reveals which cells are BECOMING
resistant before they fully are. This is our Time Machine.

