**Layer 4: Pathway --- Signaling Cascades, Feedback Loops, Escape
Routes**

**What it captures:** Every signaling pathway active in mCRPC. Crosstalk
between pathways (blocking one activates another). Known resistance
escape routes. Metabolic dependencies.

**Key mCRPC escape routes verified in literature:** (1) AR-V7 splice
variant bypasses enzalutamide/abiraterone. (2) PI3K/AKT/mTOR activation
when AR is blocked (PTEN loss in 40-60%). (3) WNT/beta-catenin in
neuroendocrine transdifferentiation. (4) Glucocorticoid receptor
substitution for AR. (5) JAK/STAT inflammatory signaling drives lineage
plasticity (Chan et al., Science 2022). (6) MYC overexpression
antagonizes AR transcriptional program, promoting CRPC progression.

