**Layer 6: Cellular --- All Cell Populations in the Tumor Ecosystem**

**What it captures:** Every cell type in mCRPC tumors and
microenvironment. Derived from scRNA-seq clustering. Critical
populations include:

**Verified mCRPC cell populations from published scRNA-seq:** (1)
AR-positive luminal adenocarcinoma (majority, treatment-sensitive). (2)
AR-negative/low cells with neuroendocrine features (resistant). (3)
Lineage plasticity cells (LPCs) --- AR-negative, stemness traits, HMMR+,
pre-existing in primary tumors, enriched in CRPC/mCRPC (eBioMedicine
2024). (4) CRPC-like cells expressing TOP2A, NUSAP1, PHGR1 ---
pre-existing adaptive cells that clonally expand during progression. (5)
Cancer-associated fibroblasts (CAFs) --- secrete growth factors
promoting resistance, TGF-beta pathway. (6) SPP1hi tumor-associated
macrophages (SPP1hi-TAMs) --- enriched in mCRPC progression, suppress
CD8+ T cells via adenosine signaling (Nature 2024). (7) Exhausted CD8+ T
cells. (8) Regulatory T cells. (9) NK cells. (10) Endothelial cells
(including activated ECs communicating with tumor). (11) Normal
epithelial cells (for selectivity comparison).

**Why LPCs and SPP1hi-TAMs matter for INTERCEPTA:** LPCs are the
pre-resistant population our Time Machine must detect. SPP1hi-TAMs
explain why mCRPC is immunologically cold. Any drug combination must
account for both.

