**Layer 8: Clinical --- Trial Outcomes, Biomarkers, PSA Kinetics**

**What it captures:** Clinical trial outcomes (our 5 ground truth
trials + all other mCRPC trials). Biomarker-outcome associations. PSA
kinetics data that constrains ODE growth rates. Real-world treatment
sequencing.

**PSA doubling time data (verified from literature):** In aggressive
mCRPC, PSA doubling time (PSADT) \< 4 months is associated with rapid
progression and poor survival. PSADT \< 10 months marks clinically
significant disease. In untreated organ-confined prostate cancer, 79% of
patients have PSADT \> 24 months (Schmid et al., Cancer 1993). In mCRPC
on treatment, growth rate constants from NCI trials showed 10-fold
slower growth with modern combination therapy compared to single-agent
approaches (Stein et al., PMC6667189).

**Biomarker-outcome edges (verified):** BRCA2 loss predicts olaparib
response (PROfound). RB1 alteration is the strongest predictor of poor
outcome in mCRPC (Abida et al. 2019). AR-V7 splice variant predicts
enzalutamide/abiraterone resistance. TP53+RB1 co-loss drives
neuroendocrine transdifferentiation.

